# endings — win, fail, and end story conditions

verb seize
    takes noun
    "You can't seize that."

verb quaff
    takes noun
    "Nothing to quaff."

verb study
    takes noun
    "Nothing to study."

room Tavern "A dusty tavern."

    object trophy "A golden trophy."

        instead of seize:
            win "You seize the trophy and claim victory!"

    object poison "A vial of poison."

        instead of quaff:
            fail "The poison takes hold. Everything goes dark."

    object note "A crumpled note."

        instead of study:
            end story "The note reads: this story has no ending."

test "win"
    seize trophy. "You seize the trophy"

test "fail"
    quaff poison. "The poison takes hold"

test "end story"
    study note. "this story has no ending"
